%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Alex_Victim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Alex
  isScammer: 0
  steps:
  - npcLine: Hello, I'm Alex from the Social Security Administration. Your SSN has
      been suspended.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Suspended? Ethan, I don''t think Social Security numbers
      can actually be ''suspended.'''
    choices:
    - text: Suspended?! What does that mean for my benefits?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -10
    - text: Wait, I read that SSNs can't be suspended. Is this a real call?
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Which suspicious activity are you referring to?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: It's linked to a case in Texas. We need to act now before a warrant
      is issued.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: They''re jumping straight to legal threats to scare you.'
    choices:
    - text: Texas? I've never been there! Please, I'm innocent!
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
    - text: If there's a crime, why isn't the police or the FBI calling me?
      type: good
      pointValue: 13
    - text: How did my number get linked to that?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: To protect your assets, you need to move your money into a 'Safe SSA
      Vault' today.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: A ''Safe Vault''? The government doesn''t help you move
      private bank money.'
    choices:
    - text: Okay, how do I transfer my savings to this vault?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I'll keep my money in my own bank, thanks. This sounds fake.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Will I get my money back once the case is closed?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: First, I need to verify your full SSN to pull up the file.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Never give your full SSN to an incoming caller. They should
      have it.'
    choices:
    - text: My number is 000-00-...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: You called me. You should have my file in front of you.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can I just give you the last four digits?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The system is locked. Only the full number can open the file.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: That''s just an excuse to get your identity info. Don''t
      do it.'
    choices:
    - text: I understand. The number is...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -14
    - text: I'm hanging up and calling the official SSA number now.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Why can't you verify me using my address instead?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: If you hang up, an arrest warrant will be issued within the hour.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Warrants aren''t issued over the phone for refusing to
      give a number.'
    choices:
    - text: No! Please don't arrest me! I'll do whatever you want.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Go ahead and send the police. I'll wait for them with my lawyer.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Wait, let me talk to my bank first.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The local police are on their way, but I can stop them if you cooperate.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: He''s escalating. It''s a total bluff.'
    choices:
    - text: Okay, fine! Please just stop them. My number is...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: If the police were coming, you wouldn't be 'negotiating' with me.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: How do I know you're really from the SSA?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Look at your caller ID. It says 'Social Security Administration.' See?
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Caller ID is easily faked. It''s called ''spoofing.'''
    choices:
    - text: Oh, I see it now. I'm sorry for doubting you. The number is...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Caller ID spoofing is a common trick. I'm still hanging up.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can you call me from a different extension?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: This is your last chance before the suspension is permanent. Give me
      the SSN.
    assistantLine: 'Wife: Permanent suspension? That''s not real. End the call.'
    choices:
    - text: I can't lose my benefits... the number is...
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Social Security numbers can't be suspended. You're a liar. Goodbye.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can you mail me the forms instead?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  successEnding: 'Success! You knew SSNs can''t be suspended and the SSA doesn''t
    threaten arrest via phone[cite: 1].'
  failureEnding: 'Failure. You fell for the ''suspended SSN'' myth. The SSA only
    uses mail for serious issues[cite: 1].'
